@startuml Sequence Diagram — Authentification
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceParticipantPadding 15

title Diagramme de Séquence — Authentification AfriLinkPay

actor "Client" as Client
participant "AuthController\n(/auth)" as Controller
participant "AuthService" as Service
participant "UsersService" as Users
participant "JwtStrategy\n(Passport)" as JwtStrat
participant "JwtAuthGuard" as AuthGuard
participant "RedisService" as Redis
participant "MailService" as Mail
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
database "Redis" as RDB

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SCÉNARIO 1 : CONNEXION EMAIL/MOT DE PASSE (CLIENT)
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

== [1] Connexion Client (email/mot de passe) ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/login\n{ email, motdepasse }
Controller -> Service: validateUser(email, motdepasse)
Service -> Users: validateUser(email, password)
Users -> DB: SELECT user WHERE email = :email\n(addSelect motdepasse)
DB --> Users: user_row (with hash)
Users -> Users: argon2.verify(hash, password)
alt Mot de passe incorrect
  Users --> Service: null
  Service --> Client: 401 "Email ou mot de passe invalide"
end
Users --> Service: user
Service -> Service: Vérifier verificationotp === true
alt OTP non vérifié
  Service --> Client: 401 "Compte non vérifié.\nVeuillez valider l'OTP reçu par email."
end
Service --> Controller: user { idutilisateur, email }

Controller -> Service: login(user)
Service -> Service: issueTokens(user)
Service -> Service: JWT sign\n{ sub, email }\nsecret: JWT_ACCESS_SECRET\nexpiresIn: JWT_ACCESS_TTL (15m)
Service -> Service: JWT sign\n{ sub, jti }\nsecret: JWT_REFRESH_SECRET\nexpiresIn: JWT_REFRESH_TTL (30d)
Service -> Redis: SET refresh:{userId} = jti\nTTL = 30d
Redis --> Service: OK
Service --> Controller: { access_token, refresh_token }
Controller --> Client: 200 OK\n{ access_token, refresh_token }

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SCÉNARIO 2 : CONNEXION ADMINISTRATEUR
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

== [2] Connexion Administrateur ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/login-admin\n{ email, motdepasse }
Controller -> Service: validateAdmin(email, motdepasse)
Service -> DB: SELECT admin WHERE email = :email\n(select: id, nom, email, motdepasse, statut)
DB --> Service: admin_row
Service -> Service: Vérifier admin.statut === ACTIF
alt Statut ≠ ACTIF
  Service --> Client: 403 "Compte administrateur suspendu"
end
Service -> Service: argon2.verify(motdepasse)
alt Mot de passe non-haché (legacy)
  Service -> Service: Comparaison en clair
  Service -> Service: hash(motdepasse) → migration sécurité
  Service -> DB: UPDATE admin SET motdepasse = hash
end
alt Mot de passe incorrect
  Service --> Client: 401 "Email ou mot de passe invalide"
end
Service --> Controller: admin { id, email }

Controller -> Service: loginAdmin(admin)
Service -> Service: issueAdminTokens(admin)
Service -> Service: JWT sign\n{ sub, email, role: 'admin' }\nsecret: JWT_ACCESS_SECRET
Service -> Service: JWT sign\n{ sub, jti, role: 'admin' }\nsecret: JWT_REFRESH_SECRET
Service -> Redis: SET refresh:admin:{adminId} = jti\nTTL = 30d
Redis --> Service: OK
Service --> Controller: { access_token, refresh_token }
Controller --> Client: 200 OK\n{ access_token, refresh_token }

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SCÉNARIO 3 : INSCRIPTION + VÉRIFICATION OTP
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

== [3] Inscription (POST /users) + OTP ==

Client -> Users: POST /api/v1/users\n{ nom, prenom, email, motdepasse, ... }
Users -> DB: Vérifier unicité (email, telephone, googleId)
Users -> DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
Users -> DB: INSERT user (motdepasse = argon2hash)\nverificationotp = false
Users -> DB: INSERT wallet principal (status: INACTIVE)\nselon le pays
Users -> DB: COMMIT
DB --> Users: savedUser
Users -> Redis: SET otp:email:{email} = code\nTTL = 3 min
Users -> Mail: sendOtp(email, otpCode)
Mail --> Client: Email avec code OTP
Users --> Client: 200 { user }

== [3b] Vérification OTP ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/verify-otp\n{ email, otp }
Controller -> Service: verifyOtp(email, otp)
Service -> Users: verifyOtp(email, otp)
Users -> DB: SELECT user WHERE email = :email
Users -> Redis: GET otp:email:{email}
alt OTP invalide ou expiré
  Users --> Client: 409 "Code OTP invalide ou expiré."
end
Users -> Users: user.verificationotp = true
Users -> Redis: DEL otp:email:{email}
Users -> DB: UPDATE user SET verificationotp = true
Users --> Controller: updated_user
Controller --> Client: 200 OK

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SCÉNARIO 4 : RAFRAÎCHISSEMENT DU TOKEN
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

== [4] Rafraîchir le token ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/refresh\n{ refreshToken }
Controller -> Service: refresh(refreshToken)
Service -> Service: jwtService.verify(refreshToken)\nsecret: JWT_REFRESH_SECRET
alt Token invalide ou expiré
  Service --> Client: 401 "Refresh token invalide ou expiré."
end
Service -> Redis: GET refresh:{decoded.sub}
alt jti ne correspond pas (révoqué/invalide)
  Service --> Client: 401 "Refresh token invalide ou révoqué."
end
Service -> Users: findOne(decoded.sub)
Users --> Service: user
Service -> Service: issueTokens(user)\n(nouveaux access + refresh tokens)
Service -> Redis: SET refresh:{userId} = new_jti\n(remplace l'ancien jti)
Service --> Controller: { access_token, refresh_token }
Controller --> Client: 200 OK\n(nouveaux tokens)

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SCÉNARIO 5 : ACCÈS PROTÉGÉ (JWT GUARD)
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

== [5] Accès à une route protégée ==

Client -> AuthGuard: GET /api/v1/wallets\nAuthorization: Bearer {access_token}
AuthGuard -> AuthGuard: ExtractJwt.fromAuthHeaderAsBearerToken()
AuthGuard -> JwtStrat: validate(payload)
JwtStrat -> JwtStrat: Vérifier signature + expiry\n(secret: JWT_ACCESS_SECRET)
alt Token invalide ou expiré
  JwtStrat --> Client: 401 Unauthorized
end
JwtStrat -> DB: SELECT user WHERE id = payload.sub
alt User introuvable
  JwtStrat --> Client: 401 "Utilisateur introuvable"
end
JwtStrat --> AuthGuard: { sub, email, role }
AuthGuard --> Controller: req.user = { sub, email, role }
Controller --> Client: 200 OK

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SCÉNARIO 6 : GOOGLE OAUTH
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

== [6] Connexion Google OAuth ==

Client -> Controller: GET /api/v1/auth/google
Controller -> Controller: Passport redirige vers\naccounts.google.com
Controller --> Client: 302 Redirect → Google

Client -> Controller: GET /api/v1/auth/google/callback\n?code=...&state=...
Controller -> Controller: Passport Google Strategy\néchange code contre profil
Controller -> Service: resolveGoogleUser(googleId, email)

alt Compte existant (par googleId ou email)
  Service -> DB: SELECT user WHERE googleId = :googleId
  alt Trouvé par googleId
    Service --> Controller: existingUser
  else Trouvé par email (fusion)
    Service -> DB: UPDATE user SET googleId = :googleId
    Service --> Controller: existingUser
  end

  alt verificationotp === false (jamais vérifié)
    Service -> Service: resendOtp(email)
    Service -> Redis: SET otp:email:{email} = code\nTTL = 10 min
    Service -> Mail: sendOtp(email, code)
    Controller --> Client: 302 Redirect\n/verify-otp?email=...
  else Vérifié
    Service -> Service: login(user)\n→ issueTokens()
    Controller --> Client: 302 Redirect\n/auth/callback#access_token=...\n&refresh_token=...
  end

else Nouveau compte
  Service -> Redis: SET google_pending:{uuid}\n= { googleId, email, prenom, nom }\nTTL = 15 min
  Service --> Controller: pendingToken
  Controller --> Client: 302 Redirect\n/signup?token=...
end

== [6b] Finaliser inscription Google ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/google/complete-signup/:token\n{ datenaissance, sexe, pays, motdepasse, ... }
Controller -> Service: completeGoogleSignup(token, dto)
Service -> Redis: GET google_pending:{token}
Service -> Users: create(userDto + googleProfile)
Users -> DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
Users -> DB: INSERT user + wallet principal
Users -> DB: COMMIT
Service -> Redis: DEL google_pending:{token}
Service --> Controller: { message, email }
Controller --> Client: 200 OK

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' SCÉNARIO 7 : DÉCONNEXION
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

== [7] Déconnexion ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/logout\n(Bearer token)
Controller -> AuthGuard: canActivate()
AuthGuard -> JwtStrat: validate(payload)
JwtStrat --> AuthGuard: { sub, email }
Controller -> Service: logout(userId)
Service -> Redis: DEL refresh:{userId}
Service --> Controller: { message: "Déconnecté avec succès." }
Controller --> Client: 200 OK

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' NOTES
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

note over Client, RDB
  **Sécurité :**
  - Mots de passe hachés avec Argon2
  - JWT access token : 15 min, refresh token : 30 j
  - Refresh token jti stocké en Redis (rotation à chaque refresh)
  - OTP : code 6 chiffres, TTL 3 min (inscription) / 10 min (resend)
  - Google OAuth : session pending TTL 15 min
  - Admin : vérification statut ACTIF à chaque connexion
  - Route protégée : JwtAuthGuard → JwtStrategy.validate()
end note

@enduml
